Physicians should provide Medicaid-covered fluoride varnish **from tooth eruption until the beneficiary is 3½ years old**. The varnish code is limited to beneficiaries **under 3½ years of age**, may be billed **once every 60 calendar days**, and is limited to **six applications before the child reaches 3½**. [[Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), effective 12/4/2019]

## Oral screening requirements

North Carolina Medicaid’s physician fluoride varnish policy requires:

- **Early caries screening** and detection of notable findings in the oral cavity using **a dental mirror and directed light**;
- **Counseling and educational materials** on good oral hygiene practices and nutrition for children;
- **Prescribing a fluoride supplement, if indicated**;
- **Application of fluoride varnish to all erupted primary teeth**, beginning at eruption until age 3½. [[Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), § 7.2, effective 12/4/2019]

## Required documentation in the health record

The beneficiary’s record must document:

- **the oral evaluation and any notable findings**;
- **preventive oral health and dietary counseling with the primary caregiver**;
- **application of fluoride varnish**; and
- **referral to a dentist, if appropriate**. [[Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), § 7.2, effective 12/4/2019]

## Visit timing example in the policy

The policy’s example table shows oral screening preventive package visits at well-child visits around **6, 9, 12, 18, 24, and 36 months** (with the 6- and 9-month visits if teeth have erupted). [[Physician Fluoride Varnish Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/1a-23-physician-fluoride-varnish-services/download?attachment), “Example of Oral Screening Preventive Package Visits,” effective 12/4/2019]

